          "We do not collect your email address, friends, messages, private repositories, payment details or other activity on these services.",
          "How the copy stays current. Steam and GitHub: only when you link or press Refresh. Each Refresh replaces the earlier copy; we keep no history. So a game, repository or text you change or remove there stays here until you press Refresh. If GitHub no longer knows your account when you press Refresh, we delete the link. Twitch: Twitch allows us to keep its data for at most 24 hours, so our server reads your Twitch name, picture, description, Partner or Affiliate status and channel category again every day. Anything that could not be checked for 24 hours is no longer shown and is deleted from our copy within the next hour; only your Twitch id stays. If Twitch no longer knows your account, we delete the link. So that we can show when you are live, our server asks Twitch to send us a short message when your channel goes live or offline; for this, Twitch receives your channel id from us. If you remove Zrzur in your Twitch settings, Twitch tells us and we delete the link. Battle.net: Blizzard allows us to keep its data for at most 30 days, so your BattleTag shows for 30 days after you sign in there through Zrzur. To keep it longer, press \"Confirm on Battle.net\" before then and sign in there again; otherwise we delete it.",
          "Pictures. Game pictures, achievement icons and profile pictures from these services are fetched through our own link service when someone views your profile. Neither you nor people who view your profile connect to these services, and their IP addresses are not sent there. We do not store these pictures: our server keeps them in memory for up to 1 minute, and the viewer's browser may keep them for up to 10 minutes.",
          "Valve, Twitch, GitHub and Blizzard are separate companies, each responsible for its own data under its own privacy policy; they are not our service providers. Each can see that your account was linked to Zrzur. Names, descriptions and other texts come from those services and their users. Steam achievement names and descriptions are shown in English, as Steam gives them; other texts in the language their authors used. Bots never receive your linked accounts.",
